TITLE:: ParaEQPanel
summary:: an eq's controls as one view
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/ParaEQ, Classes/ParaEQGUI, Classes/ParaEQView, Classes/ParaEQSpectrum, Classes/FxHintBar

DESCRIPTION::
What every window that shows an eq is built from: the eq's own window, the
compressor's sidechain page, the master chain in ServerPanel, the module family's
eq tab.

code::
 [x] eq on  [x] spectrum  preset [warm v] [flat]  [name   ][save][delete]   [copy][paste]
 +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
 |  the curve, seven handles, the analysis behind them                          |
 +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
 [low shelf][peak 1][peak 2][peak 3][high shelf][high pass][low pass]
                              freq [ 80] dB [-6.0] q [0.80] [x] in
::

The last two handles are the cuts. code::in:: is their switch and the one
control in the row that only they have: a band is always in, and it is its gain
that says what it does. The dB box greys out while a cut is selected, since a
cut has no gain.

It follows one link::Classes/ParaEQ:: and can be pointed at another, which is
how a module window shows the eq of whichever pad is selected:

code::
panel = ParaEQPanel(eq);
window.layout = VLayout(panel.view, hints.view);
panel.hints = hints;          // labels every control
panel.running = true;         // the analysis, while the panel is showing
panel.eq = otherEq;
panel.remove;                 // in window.onClose
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: eq
ARGUMENT:: parent
ARGUMENT:: subject
What the hints call the thing being shaped - "this pad", "the sidechain".
ARGUMENT:: showOnBox
code::false:: leaves the on switch out, for a window that has one of its own.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: eq
The eq shown. The view, the analyser and the boxes all follow it.

METHOD:: view
The panel.

METHOD:: eqView
The link::Classes/ParaEQView:: in the middle.

METHOD:: spectrum
The link::Classes/ParaEQSpectrum:: behind the curve.

METHOD:: running
Whether the analysis runs. A window sets it while the panel is showing.

METHOD:: hints
A link::Classes/FxHintBar:: to label every control.

METHOD:: selected
The handle the boxes are on - one of the five bands, or one of the two cuts.

METHOD:: refresh

METHOD:: remove
Stops listening to the eq and frees the analyser. In the window's onClose.
